---
/**
 * Card-tier rewrite (2026-08) from owner-supplied project facts. Card
 * spine: h1 claim + one Overview block + hero video + one prototype
 * clip. No metrics exist for this project — the outcome is the internal
 * pilot, stated qualitatively.
 *
 * The only case study using CaseStudyLayout's named "hero" slot instead
 * of `heroImage`: the hero is a YouTube `<iframe>`, not a background
 * image. `class="hero"` goes on the wrapping div so HeroImage's
 * `:global(.hero)` rule gives it `height: 100%`.
 *
 * Sizing (a11y fix, 2026-07-30): no attribute sizing on the embed —
 * scoped CSS (`width/height: 100%`) fills HeroImage's fixed-height box,
 * so the box is reserved before the iframe loads and nothing shifts.
 */
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import ContentBlock from '../../components/ContentBlock.astro';
import ContentMedia from '../../components/ContentMedia.astro';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Yandex.Run — running music case study · Jury Alyavdin"
  description="A running-music concept from Yandex's School of Mobile Design: the tempo followed the runner's live cadence. Piloted internally at Yandex with real users."
  path="/casestudy/run.html"
  h1="Music that follows the runner, not a preset playlist"
  avatarImage="/casestudy/run/run.png"
  orbitTop="Yandex.Run"
  orbitBottom="Music Streaming"
  glow="#080808"
  details={[
    { label: 'Platform', value: 'Android' },
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Product Designer' },
    { label: 'Date', value: '2016' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="hero" slot="hero">
    <iframe
      src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/3_RzI-oWqK4"
      title="Yandex.Run concept video"
      loading="lazy"
      frameborder="0"
      allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
      allowfullscreen
    ></iframe>
  </div>

  <ContentBlock title="Overview">
    <p>
      Yandex.Run was a concept for a running music service that matched music tempo to the
      runner's live cadence. I designed it in 2016 during Yandex's School of Mobile Design, and
      it was piloted internally at Yandex with real users — though never publicly released.
    </p>
    <p>
      The School took participants from an idea through to launch; in the second stage, teams
      carried out a joint project with managers and developers. Our project set out to find
      product-market fit for a new service built on the radio-streaming technology behind
      Yandex.Music. I was the sole designer on the team and owned the design end to end —
      concept, UI, motion, and brand. The defining call: track the runner's cadence live and let
      the music follow it, rather than serve fixed-tempo playlists picked by pace band before
      the run.
    </p>
    <p><strong class="lead-in">Piloted inside Yandex, never released:</strong> the concept ran as a working prototype.</p>
    <ContentMedia kind="video" src="/casestudy/run/run" alt="Screen recording of the Yandex.Run prototype player matching music to running pace" width={640} height={370} />
  </ContentBlock>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<style>
  /* No aspect-ratio here: HeroImage's box already has definite heights
     (620/400/320) and .hero fills it; adding a ratio makes the width
     compute FROM the height and overflow the viewport on mobile. */
  .hero iframe {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
  }
</style>
